    "body": "### Update: Custom Elements Parity Approach\n\nAfter thinking about @Kaiido's feedback and researching existing patterns, I realized there's already precedent for this in Custom Elements:\n\n[Custom Elements](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web_components/Using_custom_elements#custom_element_lifecycle_callbacks) already have this:\n```js\nconnectedCallback() { /* element connected to DOM */ }\ndisconnectedCallback() { /* element removed from DOM */ }\n```\n\nIt would extend these lifecycle events to ALL HTML elements, not just Custom Elements.\n\n#### Benefits:\n\n- Leverages existing browser infrastructure\n- Solves the \"element connected + layout available\" problem\n- Makes lifecycle events a universal HTML feature, not just a Custom Elements privilege\n\n#### Suggested Implementation:\n\n- onconnected / ondisconnected attributes for all elements\n- connected / disconnected events for addEventListener\n- Developer can combine with requestAnimationFrame() for layout timing\n\n\nExample:\n```js\n// as event listener\nelement.addEventListener('connected', function() {\n  requestAnimationFrame(() => {\n    console.log(element.offsetHeight, element.offsetWidth);\n    initCollapse(element);\n  });\n});\n\n// as HTML Attribute\n<div onconnected=\"requestAnimationFrame(() => initCollapse(this))\">\n```\n",
